//Eyes
# Almond eyes with gently lowered lids for her calm smile. For an eye, xi runs from the inner corner
# (-1) to the outer corner (+1); eu and el are the upper and lower lid heights above the eye line.
# ecl clips a height between the lids, so the upper lid hides the top of the iris. Layers, back to front:
# eye white and the lid's shadow on it, iris (amber, darkening toward the top, golden below), the radial
# pattern around the pupil and light streaks, rim, pupil, highlights, then lashes, crease and brow.
eu(xi)=0.012+0.16*(1-min(1,xi^2))^0.55-0.025*min(xi,1)+0.02*xi*(1-min(1,xi^2))
el(xi)=-0.085*(1-min(1,xi^2))^0.7-0.015*min(xi,1)
ecl(xi,hh)=max(el(xi),min(eu(xi),hh))
lt(xi)=(0.016+0.03*min(1,max(0,(xi+0.2)/1.0)))*min(1,(xi+1)/0.3)^0.5*min(1,max(0,1.3-xi)/0.3)^0.8
ltop(xi)=eu(min(xi,1))-0.06*max(0,xi-1)+lt(xi)
(0.37+0.215*xi,qeL(0.37+0.215*xi,11.79+el(xi)+eta*(eu(xi)-el(xi)))-0.004,11.79+el(xi)+eta*(eu(xi)-el(xi)),xi,(-1),1,eta,0,1) | ref=eyeWhiteL color=#f6f3f8
(0.37+0.215*xi,qeL(0.37+0.215*xi,11.79+eu(xi)-eta*0.05*(1-min(1,xi^2))^0.4)-0.005,11.79+eu(xi)-eta*0.05*(1-min(1,xi^2))^0.4,eta,0,1,xi,(-1),1) | ref=lidShadowL color=#d9cdda
