# Hanging strands (sidelocks, back hair): a centre line (polynomial in s, from a Bezier curve) with a
# horizontal lens cross-section, half-width hw(s)*a and half-thickness ht(s)*b, turned by angle al.
hw(s)=(1-s)^0.75*(0.7+0.3*min(1,4*s))*(1.15-0.2*s)
ht(s)=(1-s)^0.4*(0.6+0.4*min(1,4*s))

//Hair ornament: chrysanthemum on a black bow, cream ribbons, gold tassel
# Bow loop in local coordinates: s 0..1 from the knot outward, w around; length le, half-height he,
# half-thickness te. The loop is pinched at the knot and rounded at the end.
bla(s,le)=le*s
blh(s,w,he)=he*sin(pi*s)^0.55*(0.35+0.65*s)*cos(w)
blt(s,w,te)=te*sin(pi*s)^0.5*sin(w)
